HIRID-ICU-Benchmark (https://github.com/ratschlab/HIRID-ICU-Benchmark). The names of HiRID's pharma items in
cohorts/abx_sets.py are those of its variable reference (preprocessing/resources/varref.tsv). Under the MIT
License, whose text is given at the end of this file:

Copyright (c) 2021, ETH Zurich, Biomedical Informatics Group; ratschlab

OHDSI Common Data Model (https://github.com/OHDSI/CommonDataModel, Apache License 2.0).
omop_etl/schema/OMOP_CDMv5.4_Field_Level.csv is its inst/csv/OMOP_CDMv5.4_Field_Level.csv of v5.4.0, modified: the
field name offset of NOTE_NLP is unquoted (line 221), and the line endings are LF.

OHDSI MIMIC (https://github.com/OHDSI/MIMIC, Apache License 2.0). The measurement concepts of omop_etl/mappings
follow the concepts its MIMIC-IV ETL assigns (omop_etl/docs/OHDSI-MIMIC.md).

ricu (https://github.com/eth-mds/ricu; Bennett et al., "ricu: R's interface to intensive care data", GigaScience
2023, doi:10.1093/gigascience/giad041; GPL-3), which builds YAIB's cohorts. The cohort rules of cohorts/ reproduce
ricu's behaviour, as we studied it in ricu's documentation, source and outputs; they are written anew in Python and
SQL and contain no ricu code. cohorts/tests/ricu_labels.py and cohorts/tests/sofa.py reproduce ricu's SOFA and
Sepsis-3 rules as references for the tests. The plausible ranges in cohorts/yaib_omop_crosswalk.py (RICU_BOUNDS) and
the SOFA thresholds are values of ricu's concept dictionary and callbacks, and most source_label descriptions of
omop_etl/mappings/eicu and omop_etl/mappings/hirid are its concept-dictionary descriptions. RICU.md lists where the
cohorts follow ricu and where they differ.

OMOP Standardized Vocabularies (OHDSI, https://athena.ohdsi.org). omop_etl/tests/fixtures/vocabulary holds the
concept ids, domains, vocabularies and classes of the concepts the demo CDMs and the mapping tables use, with names
and codes only for UCUM and the vocabularies OMOP generates itself. The UCUM codes and names: Copyright 1999-2024
Regenstrief Institute, Inc. All rights reserved. Used under the UCUM License, Version 1.1
(https://unitsofmeasure.org/license), provided "AS IS", without warranties or conditions of any kind.

MIMIC-IV Clinical Database Demo (Johnson A, Bulgarelli L, Pollard T, Horng S, Celi LA, Mark R. MIMIC-IV Clinical
Database Demo, version 2.2. PhysioNet 2023, doi:10.13026/dp1f-ex47). The stored outputs of
cohorts/notebooks/omop_ehrdata_ehrapy_pypots.ipynb contain information from the MIMIC-IV Clinical Database Demo,
which is made available under the Open Database License (ODbL) v1.0,
https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/. The MIMIC-IV item ids and labels in omop_etl/mappings/mimic4 and
cohorts/ are those of its d_items and d_labitems tables.


